    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d237">

                <pb facs="0436" n="332" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg332"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Lincoln.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-04-10"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 10,
                        1890</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 233.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch No. 203 of the 28th ultimo,
                    concerning the inconvenience to which Mr. Louis Wagner has been subjected by a
                    paper <pb facs="0437" n="333" xml:id="pg333"/> in the nature of a passport
                    issued to him by the governor of Minnesota, has been received and brought to the
                    attention of that officer.</p>
                <p>Inclosing for your information copies of correspondence relative to a similar
                    case at Vienna,</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine.</hi></signed></closer>






